                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCU15FD86</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>14024070</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U15FD86</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_74682172">VCU Communication Verification Fault</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1776433319">1.Ensure stable CAN communication            2.Ensure Correct Gateway functionallity                  3.Check the wire harness and connectors</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_64563110">1. EC-1:  Ignition Status                                                                   2. EC-2 Local Voltage                                                              3. EC-3 Bus Physical status                                                      4. EC-4 Debounce Timer             5. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 19.5) = Enabled                      6.Loss Communication with VCU should not be present</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1975618681">Message Cyclic Rate</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_106111951">DTC U15FD-86 shall be set if any of the below messages matches with below mentioned criteria,
Messages :VCU_0x214
 
 -Fails the CheckSum calculation in the last 3 consecutive messages.
OR 
 -Alive counters increment by &gt; 1 in the last 3 consecutive messages
OR
 -During normal communication between sending node and receiving node,If the alive counter value is 0xF for 3 consecutive messages.
OR
-Alive counter value is repeated in the last 3 consecutive messages
 
Each message shall be considered individually                                                                          Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_5363089">Message "VCU_0x214 ":are met with below condition
 
- Check Sum is correct
- Alive counters increment by = 1;
- Alive counter value is 0xF does not apper
- Alive counter value is not repeated                                                      Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_927047583">1. After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged
2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_323377538">1.Failure might be at VCU
2.CAN Harness Fault</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1827919209">feature degradation</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC><DTC ID="DLC.DLC_FCM.BV.BV_FCM.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC226600">
                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCC226600</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>6448640</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C226600</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_2087522592">HSM/SW Algorithm initialization Failure</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>1</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1165604301">Hard reset is required</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_2022887155">1. EC-1:  Ignition Status                                                                   2. EC-2 Local Voltage                                                              3. EC-3 Bus Physical status                                                      4. EC-4 Debounce Timer             5. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 19.6) = Enabled </SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_672310828">During start</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_731849846">The component shall set the DTC Immediately if the return value of HSM/SW Algorithm initialization failed or unsuccessful. Since initialization happens at the startup, the Failure will be latched until the same HSM initialization function is called again (i.e. entire ECU power cycle).
Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_241654147">The component shall not set any DTC if the HSM initialization is Passed or successful
Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_991373827">1. Power cycle with DTC pass criteria After that 40 Drive cycles to be performed.
2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1210134228">HSM/SW Algorithm initialization failed or unsuccessful</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1651746936">ECU shall not be able to offer the HSM services.</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC><DTC ID="DLC.DLC_FCM.BV.BV_FCM.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC226700">
                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCC226700</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>6448896</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C226700</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_1876940853">Keys [Symmetric key/Key-Raw] corrupted</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>2</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1686051271">No repair action</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_683854437">1. EC-1:  Ignition Status                                                                   2. EC-2 Local Voltage                                                              3. EC-3 Bus Physical status                                                      4. EC-4 Debounce Timer             5. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 4.1) = Enabled      </SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_533095110">During Start up &amp; Key Load</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_220289933">The component shall set the DTC Immediately if any of the below listed conditions occurs:(a) Key Storage into Memory Failed because of Encryption failed.(b) Key retrieval from Memory Failed (Example CRC/Checksum/Hash/Decryption failed)(c) All bytes of Raw_Key are either 0x00 (initial value) or 0xFF.(d) Loading the Key to HSM or equivalent function failed.The Failure will be latched (i.e. Entire ECU power cycle) until valid keys are updated.
Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1457084647">The component shall not set any DTC if the ECU is able to read and write the key-raw successfully from it's memory
Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_927047583">1. After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged
2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_675626252">1.Key storage failure                                          2. Key retrieval failure                            3. If all bytes of Raw_key are with 0x00 or 0xFF                                   4. Loading of key to HSM failure</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1540495132">FCM shall not be able to Verify and Generate the MAC for the CAN and Ethernet Signals.</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC><DTC ID="DLC.DLC_FCM.BV.BV_FCM.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC226D00">
                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCC226D00</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>6450432</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C226D00</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_906375646">MAC Generation/Verification Fail for Ethernet SecOC</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>2</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1686051271">No repair action</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_159665677">1. EC-1:  Ignition Status                                                                   2. EC-2 Local Voltage                                                              3. EC-3 Bus Physical status                                                      4. EC-4 Debounce Timer             5. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 4.7) = Enabled</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_875371230">Always</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_148747012">The component shall set the DTC If Secured PDU failed to verify within 0.7 ms (main frequency:80MHz)
OR
MAC Generation or verification fails for 3 consecutive messages.
Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1211022859">The component shall clear the DTC immediately If MAC Generation/Verification is successful once.                                                    Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_927047583">1. After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged
2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_622248221">If Secured PDU can't be verified within 0.7 ms (main frequency:80MHz) 
OR
If MAC Generation or verification fails for 3 consecutive messages.</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_2076532766">FCM shall not be able to correctly verify/Generate the Received/transmited Ethernet PDUs.</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC><DTC ID="DLC.DLC_FCM.BV.BV_FCM.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCU15E686">
                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCU15E686</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>14018182</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U15E686</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_1020226258">ESP Communication Verification Fault  (Electronic Stability Program)</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1304112743">1.Ensure stable CAN communication                                2.Ensure Correct Gateway functionallity                                            3.Check the wire harness and connectors</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_618408213">1. EC-1:  Ignition Status                                                                   2. EC-2 Local Voltage                                                              3. EC-3 Bus Physical status                                                      4. EC-4 Debounce Timer 
5. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 18.0) = Enabled            6.Loss Communication with ESP DTC should not be present</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1975618681">Message Cyclic Rate</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1421087010">DTC U15E6-86 shall be set if any of the below messages matcheds with belo mentioned criteria,
ESP_0x318 OR ESP_0x114
 
 
-Fails the CheckSum calculation in the last 3 consecutive messages.
OR 
 -Alive counters increment by &gt; 1 in the last 3 consecutive messages
OR
 -During normal communication between sending node and receiving node,If the alive counter value is 0xF for 3 consecutive messages.
OR
-Alive counter value is repeated in the last 3 consecutive messages
 
Each message shall be considered individually.     Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1595123078">Messages "ESP_0x318 AND ESP_0x114": are met with below condition:

 
- Check Sum is correct
- Alive counters increment by = 1;
- Alive counter value is 0xF  does not appear
- Alive counter value is not repeated                                                                   Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_785436229">1. After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged           2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1734952666">1.Failure might be at ESP             2.CAN Harness Fault</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1827919209">feature degradation</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC><DTC ID="DLC.DLC_FCM.BV.BV_FCM.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCU15E986">
                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCU15E986</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>14018950</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U15E986</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_1493481507">YRS Communication Verification Fault</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_999663277">1.Ensure stable CAN communication            2.Ensure Correct Gateway functionallity                          3.Check the wire harness and connectors</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_540361128">1. EC-1:  Ignition Status                                                                   2. EC-2 Local Voltage                                                              3. EC-3 Bus Physical status                                                      4. EC-4 Debounce Timer 
5. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 18.3) = Enabled           6.Loss of communication with YRS DTC should not be present </SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1975618681">Message Cyclic Rate</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_364927776">DTC U15E9-86 shall be set if any of the below messages matches with below mentioned criteria,
Messages :YRS_0x112
 
 -Fails the CheckSum calculation in the last 3 consecutive messages.
OR 
 -Alive counters increment by &gt; 1 in the last 3 consecutive messages
OR
 -During normal communication between sending node and receiving node,If the alive counter value is 0xF for 3 consecutive messages.
OR
-Alive counter value is repeated in the last 3 consecutive messages
 
Each message shall be considered individually.                         Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1546347104">Message "YRS_0x112":are met with below condition 
 
- Check Sum is correct
- Alive counters increment by = 1;
- Alive counter value is 0xF for 3 consecutive messages does not appear
- Alive counter value is not repeated                                                             Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_244092903">1. After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged             2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1858341521">1.Failure might be at YRS             2.CAN Harness Fault</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1827919209">feature degradation</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC><DTC ID="DLC.DLC_FCM.BV.BV_FCM.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC220C00">
                  <SHORT-NAME>DTCC220C00</SHORT-NAME>
                  <TROUBLE-CODE>6425600</TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C220C00</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                  <TEXT TI="TI_1948859123">Production Mode active</TEXT>
                  <LEVEL>1</LEVEL>
                  <SDGS>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO"><SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_353131875">Check at Next halt</SD><SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_182599615">Production mode has to be disabled</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_108416652">1. EC-1 Ignition Status (14191776)                                             2. EC-2 Local Voltage (14191778)                                        3. EC-3 Bus Physical status (14191780)                              4. EC-5 DTC Deactivation Bit Mask (Byte.Bit 0.0 ) = Enabled (12778967)    </SD><SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD><SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_875371230">Always</SD><SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1683434349">The component shall set the DTC Immediately if
DID 0x4904 = 0x6A
Maturity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1115153966">The component shall remove the DTC Immediately if
DID 0x4904 = 0x4D                                                   Dematurity time:  Immediately</SD><SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD><SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_927047583">1. After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged
2.After Getting Clear Diagnostics service request ($14)</SD><SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_230587864">Production mode is active</SD><SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_2041742987">ECU shall not have secured access</SD></SDG></SDGS>
                </DTC></DTCS>
                        </DTC-DOP>
                    </DTC-DOPS>
